  "context": [
    "Q3 2026: three consecutive deficit months (about 84,000 mt LCE cumulative) while prices fell stepwise; inventory destocking of about 68,000 mt filled the deficit, so inventory acted as a buffer rather than letting the deficit clear through price.",
    "Destocking is downstream-led: over 13 weeks to early October total inventory fell 30%+, cathode-plant stocks nearly halved, smelter stocks fell nearly 40%, while the trader share rose from under 30% to over one-third. SMM says ownership is shifting from consumers to producers and traders - a latent supply overhang.",
    "SMM revised its weekly inventory scope from 4 Sep 2026 (title-based, adds trading segment and battery-cell makers), backdated to 30 Apr 2026. Do not compare levels across the break.",
    "Cathode output stays high: LFP about 141,600 t/week, ternary about 18,000 t/week and down nine straight weeks. LFP alone implies about 34,000 t LCE/week of carbonate use, above reported cathode-plant carbonate inventory.",
    "China spodumene imports were about 970,100 t in September (+7% m/m), Zimbabwe about 136,000 t (+83%). Port stocks stay high while carbonate stocks fall: the lag runs through port storage, refinery feed and conversion, and refiners can slow withdrawals when margins compress.",
    "GFEX receipts: down 17,378 t since early September (Mysteel) but +2,040 t on Nov 9 and +50 t on Nov 10 - watch whether the drawdown has stalled.",
    "Nov 17: LC2701 rallied to 93,180 on lower open interest (short covering) while spot kept falling.",
    "Cochilco forecasts 2026 lithium demand 2.08 Mt LCE vs supply 2.0 Mt (79,000 t deficit) and a Q4 average price near US$19,000/t - far above current spot of about US$13,700/t, so treat that forecast with caution.",
    "Supply restarts: Bald Hill, Finniss; Rio Tinto spending $1.4bn on Fenix 1B and Sal de Vida."
